{"name":"Oak Barrel","hex":"#715636","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oak","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Noakhali."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deciduous tree with distinctive deeply lobed leaves, acorns, and notably strong wood, typically of England and northeastern North America, included in genus Quercus.","The wood of the oak."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oak"},{"term":"barrel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A round (cylindrical) vessel, such as a cask, of greater length than breadth, and bulging in the middle, made of staves bound with hoops, and having flat ends (heads). The word is sometimes applied to a similar cylindrical container made of metal, usually called a drum.","Such a cask of a certain size, holding one-eighth of what a tun holds. (See a diagram comparing cask sizes.)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put or to pack in a barrel or barrels.","To move quickly or in an uncontrolled manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barrel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oak (wine)","blocks":[{"text":"Oak is used in winemaking to vary the color, flavor, tannin profile and texture of wine. It can be introduced in the form of a barrel during the fermentation or aging periods, or as free-floating chips or staves added to wine fermented in a vessel like stainless steel. Oak barrels can impart other qualities to wine through evaporation and low level exposure to oxygen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Wine_Barrels.jpg/330px-Wine_Barrels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak_(wine)","wikidata":"Q808963"},{"title":"Oak","blocks":[{"text":"An oak is a hardwood tree or shrub in the genus Quercus of the beech family. They have spirally arranged leaves, often with lobed edges, and a nut called an acorn, borne within a cup. The genus is widely distributed in the Northern Hemisphere, with some 475 species, both deciduous and evergreen. Fossil oaks date back to the Middle Eocene. Molecular phylogeny shows that the genus is divided into Old World and New World clades, but many oak species hybridise freely, making the genus's history difficult to resolve."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Quercus_robur.jpg/330px-Quercus_robur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak","wikidata":"Q12004"},{"title":"Barrel","blocks":[{"text":"A barrel or cask is a hollow cylindrical container with a bulging center, longer than it is wide. They are traditionally made of wooden staves and bound by wooden or metal hoops. The word vat is often used for large containers for liquids, usually alcoholic beverages; a small barrel or cask is known as a keg."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/330px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barrel","wikidata":"Q10289"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Barrel_fermented_California_Chard.jpg/500px-Barrel_fermented_California_Chard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Barrel_fermented_California_Chard.jpg/1280px-Barrel_fermented_California_Chard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Barrel_fermented_California_Chard.jpg/500px-Barrel_fermented_California_Chard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A California Chardonnay that shows on the label that it has been barrel fermented.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarrel_fermented_California_Chard.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Oakagingcolour.jpg/500px-Oakagingcolour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Oakagingcolour.jpg/1280px-Oakagingcolour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Oakagingcolour.jpg/500px-Oakagingcolour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The effect of oak aging on two Penedès region Cabernet Sauvignon varietals, a two-year-old cosecha (left) and six-year-old crianza (right). As the wine matures, its color shifts from deep purple or crimson to a lighter brick-red, and takes on a more graduated appearance in the glass.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOakagingcolour.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/FLOR-ValdiviaJerez59.jpg/500px-FLOR-ValdiviaJerez59.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/FLOR-ValdiviaJerez59.jpg/1280px-FLOR-ValdiviaJerez59.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/FLOR-ValdiviaJerez59.jpg/500px-FLOR-ValdiviaJerez59.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Oak barrel aging sherry. It has a transparent front in order to show the process inside","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFLOR-ValdiviaJerez59.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Ch%C3%AAne_02.jpg/500px-Ch%C3%AAne_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Ch%C3%AAne_02.jpg/500px-Ch%C3%AAne_02.jpg?utm_s